    "narrative": "The offensive outlook for LawDog today centers on **Jonathan Aranda** and **Bryson Stott**, who anchor our starting unit with efficiency scores of 67.02 and 62.69, respectively. **Jonathan Aranda** is our primary target against Lugo, as the combination of a favorable 4.55 xERA and a significant +12% dynamic platoon boost makes him the most reliable engine in the lineup. While **Cal Raleigh** (61.29) and **Lawrence Butler** (62.36) also clear the 60-point threshold, **Lawrence Butler** is particularly intriguing; despite the slight park penalty, his strong platoon split against the right-handed Roupp and favorable wind conditions out provide a high floor for home run production. **Matt Chapman** also earns a recommendation today, leveraging a +10% order bonus from the leadoff spot to overcome a projected tough matchup against Springs.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today involves **Jung Hoo Lee**, who sits at a 49.89 efficiency score\u2014hovering just below the \"Strong\" start threshold. While he benefits from the same favorable wind conditions as **Lawrence Butler**, his negative platoon split against Springs ultimately suppressed his projection, making him our most marginal start. We are closely monitoring the 42% rain risk at the venues hosting **Masyn Winn** and **Geraldo Perdomo**; if these games face delays or cancellations, we will be forced to pivot to our reserves, though the current depth chart is hampered by the ongoing absences of **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** and **Will Smith** on the IL.\n\nBeyond the starters, we are keeping a close eye on **Daulton Varsho**, who was excluded from the lineup today, and **Tyler Freeman**, who is unavailable due to a team off-day. As we navigate a stretch where speed is at a premium, the optimizer remains highly sensitive to the situational constraints of our bench\u2014specifically **Gleyber Torres**, **Luis Arraez**, and **Brendan Donovan**, who remain on standby should the weather reports for **Masyn Winn** deteriorate further. We will continue to evaluate the potential contributions of **Taylor Ward**, **Yainer Diaz**, **Ryan Waldschmidt**, **Dylan Beavers**, **Jeremiah Jackson**, **Gavin Sheets**, and **Drew Gilbert** as the 2026 season progresses and platoon opportunities fluctuate.",
